    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0158" n="88" xml:id="pg88"/>

                <head>No. 40.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Logan
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 20, 1882</date>.
                        (Received January 25, 1883.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under cover of this dispatch I inclose the
                    translation of an important decree emitted by the Montero Government, wherefrom
                    it will appear that notice is given of a disavowal of the right of Chili to sell
                    the guano and nitrates priorly pledged to the creditors of Peru; the intention
                    avowed to contest the sale; and the determination to cut off those creditors of
                    Peru who have entered into arrangement with the Chilian Government
                    announced.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. A. LOGAN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d40-a1.xml" xpointer="d40-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
